cription"} [:p {} "The outdoor version of men’s singles attracted a meagre field, lacking the top British, American, and Australian players.  The best British player of the era was " [:a {:href "/athletes/97"} "Arthur “Wentworth” Gore"] ", but he competed only in the covered court events.  The top American player was Bill Larned, and the top Australasians were " [:a {:href "/athletes/1805033"} "Norman Brookes"] " (AUS) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/80451"} "Tony Wilding"] " (NZL), but they did not compete."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In their absence, " [:a {:href "/athletes/113"} "Josiah Ritchie"] " won the gold medal, taking the final in four sets over the German " [:a {:href "/athletes/143"} "Otto Froitzheim"] ".  Ritchie was a good player but never the top player in the world.  His other titles in his career include: 1903-1906 and 1908 German singles; 1909 and 1914 British covered court singles; 1907 Irish singles; 1902, 1904, 1906, and 1909 London singles; 1908 and 1910 Wimbledon doubles (with Tony Wilding); 1907-07 British covered court doubles (with Tony Wilding); and the 1904 and 1906 German doubles."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/113"} "Josiah Ritchie"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143"} "Otto Froitzheim"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/